@prefix :        <https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo-sml#> .
@prefix afo:     <https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#> .
@prefix sml:     <https://w3id.org/sml/def#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@base            <https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo-sml#> .

<https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo-sml> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo-sml/0.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    rdfs:label "AFO to SML alignment" ;
    dcterms:title "Arrowhead Framework Ontology — Semantic Modelling and Linking alignment" ;
    dcterms:description "Aligns AFO's classes and properties onto SML, the top-level ontology of EN 17632 (Semantic modelling and linking), so an Arrowhead local cloud can be read beside the asset models of the built environment." ;
    dcterms:creator "Jan van Deventer" ;
    dcterms:publisher "Synecdoque" ;
    dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://docs.crow.nl/sml/> ,
                 <https://doi.org/10.1109/OJIES.2026.3693084> ;
    rdfs:comment """An alignment only, in the style of afo-lis.ttl: it introduces no
instances, and states AFO terms solely to hang alignment axioms on them. It
does not import SML; load https://w3id.org/sml/def beside it to reason.

SML declares three pairs of disjoint classes that the alignment must respect,
because a reasoner will:

  - PhysicalObject, InformationObject, Activity, Event and State;
  - FunctionalEntity and TechnicalEntity: what is needed against what
    provides it;
  - PlannedEntity and RealizedEntity: what is designed against what exists.

Functional and technical. The parts of a cloud (the cloud, its systems,
their husks, servers, unit assets and endpoints, and the hosts they run on)
are technical entities: they are the solution. What a unit asset serves, its
functional location, is the functional entity it implements. A service is
an SML function: an activity performed by an object whose external behavior
contributes to the goals of others.

Physical or not. SML's physical object exists in 4D space-time as matter or
energy. A host may be a virtual machine; a system, a husk and a unit asset
are software. They are aligned to sml:Object and no further, so they stay
consistent with either reading. afo-lis.ttl makes UnitAsset a physical
object; that is not repeated here, because a thermostat's control loop or a
weather service's forecast is not one. The endpoint is the exception: SML's
port is explicitly "a physical or logical point of interaction", and it is
aligned to that.

Planned or realized. No AFO class is aligned to either, because the class
does not decide it. The graph the kgrapher emits is observed at run time,
and its individuals are realized entities; a model of the same cloud made
before it runs, such as the modeler's SysML, describes planned ones. Typing
the individuals is the emitter's business, and sml:isRealizedBy is the
property that would link a design to what runs.

Not aligned, because SML has no counterpart: the security posture, the
external attachment, the mode of a service, and the AFO properties that
relate a service to its consumer, its endpoint and its forms. The binding of
a consumer to a provider is an SML interaction with an information-flow
transfer type over a connection; AFO has no individual for that binding to
type.""" .


#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

# Composition. Each is a technical decomposition: a technical entity made of
# technical entities, which the class alignments below make true at both ends.

###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#contains
afo:contains rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
             rdfs:subPropertyOf sml:hasTechnicalPart .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#hasHusk
afo:hasHusk rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
            rdfs:subPropertyOf sml:hasTechnicalPart .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#hasServer
afo:hasServer rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
              rdfs:subPropertyOf sml:hasTechnicalPart .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#hasUnitAsset
afo:hasUnitAsset rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf sml:hasTechnicalPart .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#hostingEndpoint
afo:hostingEndpoint rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                    rdfs:subPropertyOf sml:hasTechnicalPart ;
                    rdfs:comment "A port is part of the object it belongs to; the endpoint is the host's." .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#hasFunctionalLocation
afo:hasFunctionalLocation rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf [ owl:inverseOf sml:isImplementedBy ] ;
    rdfs:comment "SML relates the functional entity to the technical entity that implements it; a unit asset implements its functional location." .


# Units. AFO's and SML's are both sub-properties of QUDT's, with QUDT's ranges.

###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#hasUnit
afo:hasUnit rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
            rdfs:subPropertyOf sml:hasUnit .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#hasQuantityKind
afo:hasQuantityKind rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                    rdfs:subPropertyOf sml:hasQuantityKind .


# Not aligned: afo:providesService to sml:executes. SML gives executes the
# domain PhysicalObject, so the alignment would make every unit asset
# physical, which the class alignment deliberately does not.


#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#LocalCloud
afo:LocalCloud rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf sml:Object ,
                               sml:TechnicalEntity .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#System
afo:System rdf:type owl:Class ;
           rdfs:subClassOf sml:Object ,
                           sml:TechnicalEntity .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#Husk
afo:Husk rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf sml:Object ,
                         sml:TechnicalEntity .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#Server
afo:Server rdf:type owl:Class ;
           rdfs:subClassOf sml:Object ,
                           sml:TechnicalEntity .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#UnitAsset
afo:UnitAsset rdf:type owl:Class ;
              rdfs:subClassOf sml:Object ,
                              sml:TechnicalEntity .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#Host
afo:Host rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf sml:Object ,
                         sml:TechnicalEntity .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#Endpoint
afo:Endpoint rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf sml:Port ,
                             sml:TechnicalEntity .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#Service
afo:Service rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf sml:Function .


###  https://w3id.org/synecdoque/afo#FunctionalLocation
afo:FunctionalLocation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                       rdfs:subClassOf sml:FunctionalEntity .
